content.text:
Now camera occlusion. Current updateCamera:

```
const desired = new THREE.Vector3(player.x + hx, targetY + hy, player.z + hz);

// Keep the camera above the ground / out of hills.
const minY = groundHeight(desired.x, desired.z) + 0.9;
if (desired.y < minY) desired.y = minY;

if (game.cameraSnap)...
...
const lookAt = new THREE.Vector3(player.x, targetY, player.z);
camera.lookAt(lookAt);
```

Add occlusion before ground clamp maybe after. Need to compute allowed. Use lookAt target (player.x, targetY, player.z). Note desired computed from player plus offset. Use function.

Let's write:

```
  const focus = new THREE.Vector3(player.x, targetY, player.z);
  // Pull the camera in when a tree canopy sits between it and the wanderer.
  const segX = desired.x - focus.x, segZ = desired.z - focus.z;
  const segLen2 = segX * segX + segZ * segZ;
  if (segLen2 > 0.04) {
    let allowed = 1;
    for (const t of world.treeColliders) {
      const fx = focus.x - t.x, fz = focus.z - t.z;
      const b = 2 * (fx * segX + fz * segZ);
      const c = fx * fx + fz * fz - t.canopy * t.canopy;
      const disc = b * b - 4 * segLen2 * c;
      if (disc <= 0) continue;
      const k = (-b - Math.sqrt(disc)) / (2 * segLen2);
      if (k <= 0.05 || k >= allowed) continue;
      const yAt = focus.y + (desired.y - focus.y) * k;
      if (yAt < t.base || yAt > t.top) continue;
      allowed = Math.max(0.22, k - 0.04);
    }
    if (allowed < 1) {
      desired.x = focus.x + segX * allowed;
      desired.y = focus.y + (desired.y - focus.y) * allowed;
      desired.z = focus.z + segZ * allowed;
    }
  }
  // Ground clamp after occlusion.
  ...
  const lookAt = new THREE.Vector3(player.x, targetY, player.z);
```

Need min ground clamp uses desired after occlusion. Also if occlusion pulls camera close, y gets close to focus y (above player) and ground clamp might raise. Fine.

But there is a subtlety: We want to check the line from focus to desired; if focus is inside canopy (player under tree), k negative, skip; then no occlusion and camera may be inside foliage. Player can stand under trees (tree colliders radius only 0.55*s; canopy 1.55*s, so player can be under canopy edges). In that case we can't avoid. Could still pull camera. But the player under a tree canopy, camera behind likely also under foliage; blocking view. We can't fade. Not critical.

Another issue: looking up at high pitch, camera y maybe above canopy tops; skip, good.

Let's add.

input.newString:
const desired = new THREE.Vector3(player.x + hx, targetY + hy, player.z + hz);

// Pull the camera in when a tree canopy sits between it and the wanderer.
const focus = new THREE.Vector3(player.x, targetY, player.z);
const segX = desired.x - focus.x, segZ = desired.z - focus.z;
const segLen2 = segX * segX + segZ * segZ;
if (segLen2 > 0.04) {
  let allowed = 1;
